  "final_answer": "I pulled the feature list from Apple Support's \"About iOS 17 Updates\" (support.apple.com/en-us/118723, published May 13, 2025). The headline iOS 17 features, as Apple describes them:\n\n**Phone & Messages** — Contact Posters (customize how you appear on others' devices when you call); Live Voicemail with live transcription and the ability to pick up mid-message; a unified Stickers iMessage app with Live Stickers lifted from photos/videos; Check In (auto-notifies a friend or family member when you arrive safely); audio message transcription; swipe-to-reply; combined search filters; and automatic cleanup of one-time verification codes.\n\n**FaceTime** — video/audio messages when someone doesn't answer; FaceTime on Apple TV using iPhone as the camera; gesture-triggered Reactions (hearts, balloons, confetti); adjustable Studio Lighting and Portrait intensity.\n\n**StandBy** — a full-screen glanceable display when the iPhone is on its side and charging, with multiple clock styles, photo shuffling, Smart Stack widgets, Night Mode red tones, and per-MagSafe-charger preferred views.\n\n**Widgets & AirDrop** — interactive widgets you can tap to act on (e.g. complete a reminder) on Home Screen, Lock Screen and StandBy; iPhone widgets on Mac; NameDrop contact exchange and the new close-together AirDrop/SharePlay initiation.\n\n**Keyboard** — transformer-model autocorrect, easier autocorrect editing (underlined corrections you can revert with a tap), enhanced sentence corrections, and inline predictive text.\n\n**Safari & Passwords** — Profiles separating work/personal browsing; locked Private Browsing windows, tracker blocking and URL tracking removal; password and passkey sharing groups; one-time code AutoFill from Mail.\n\n**Music & AirPlay** — SharePlay for Apple Music in the car; crossfade; intelligent AirPlay device list, suggested and automatic AirPlay connections.\n\n**AirPods** — Adaptive Audio, Personalized Volume, Conversation Awareness, and press-to-mute (AirPods Pro 2nd gen with firmware 6A300+, plus press-to-mute on AirPods 3rd gen, AirPods Pro 1st/2nd gen, AirPods Max).\n\n**Maps, Siri, Visual Look Up** — Offline Maps and real-time EV charger routing; the option to just say \"Siri\" and back-to-back requests (iPhone 11 and later); expanded Visual Look Up domains, subject lifting from photos and videos, and Visual Look Up in paused video frames.\n\n**Health, Privacy, Accessibility** — State of Mind mood logging with interactive charts and mental-health assessments; Screen Distance using the TrueDepth camera; Sensitive Content Warnings and expanded Communication Safety; improved sharing permissions and Link Tracking Protection; Assistive Access, Live Speech, Personal Voice, and Point and Speak in Magnifier.\n\n**Also** — Roadside Assistance via satellite (iPhone 14/15 models only), pets in the People album, Photos Album widget, Find My item sharing with up to five people, Home Activity History and Grid Forecast, grocery lists in Reminders, full-width inline PDFs in Notes, new Memoji stickers, App Shortcuts in Spotlight, redesigned Fitness Sharing tab, email/phone-number sign-in, and new Freeform drawing tools.\n\n**iPhone 12 compatibility:** Yes — the iPhone 12 is supported by iOS 17. Apple's own feature notes in that article repeatedly qualify the new keyboard capabilities as available on \"iPhone 12 and later\" (improved autocorrect accuracy, enhanced sentence corrections, and inline predictive text), which confirms the iPhone 12 runs iOS 17 and gets those features. The iPhone 12 also meets the \"iPhone 11 and later\" bar for back-to-back Siri requests. A handful of features are hardware-limited and do NOT apply to the iPhone 12: Roadside Assistance via satellite and Crash Detection optimizations (iPhone 14/15 only), the Action button and spatial video (iPhone 15 Pro models), StandBy display-off controls (iPhone 14 Pro/15 Pro models), and Qi2 charger support (iPhone 13/14 models).\n\nOne caveat: I was not able to load Apple's dedicated \"iOS 17 is compatible with these devices\" compatibility-list article — the support search kept redirecting to other pages — so the compatibility conclusion above rests on the feature annotations inside the iOS 17 updates article rather than that standalone list. If you want the full official device roster confirmed, that article is worth opening directly.",
